# Docker build context filter (sits next to the Dockerfile).
#
# Without this file `docker build .` ships the whole working tree, including
# web/node_modules (~93 MB), local SQLite databases under data/, backups/, the
# deploy host's live state (deploy/production/data, .swarm) and any local .env
# with real secrets. None of it is needed to build the image, and some of it
# must never enter an image layer.
#
# Build inputs are exactly: go.mod/go.sum, the Go sources, web/ sources and
# web/package-lock.json. Everything else below is regenerated or irrelevant.

# VCS / agent tooling metadata
.git
.github
.opencode
.pi
.swarm
.serena
.dsh-code-index
.catalyst-code

# Secrets and local state — must never reach a build layer
.env
.env.*
token
data/
backups/

# Host-specific deployment state (the image needs nothing from deploy/)
deploy/

# Build outputs and scratch files
bin/
/gateway
models_test_output.json
reasoning_update.json
ai-gateway-playground*.html
*.bak
*.log

# Node: installed deps and generated configs. The Dockerfile's `web` stage runs
# `npm ci` itself, and host node_modules carry platform-specific esbuild/rollup
# binaries that would override the linux ones.
web/node_modules
web/dist
web/*.tsbuildinfo
web/vite.config.d.ts
web/vite.config.js

# The embedded UI is produced by the `web` stage and copied into the builder
# stage, so a committed copy must not shadow it.
cmd/gateway/web

# Caches / editor noise
vendor/
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
